WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.740
Long before he was the handsome antihero in
multiple blockbuster movies, he was a cackling

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.630
supervillain in a whole bunch of old comics.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.860
And before that, of course, he was an actual
god in mythology.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.879
Here's the untold truth of Marvel's Loki.

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:20.180
Like Thor and Odin, Loki originated in Norse
mythology, where they were all major pre-Christian

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.580
deities of the Scandinavian people.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.490
Whereas most Norse gods were big burly guys
with long beards, Loki was always portrayed

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.290
as lithe, androgynous, and sneaky.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.859
Although he was the child of Frost Giants,
he was associated with fire and the color

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:35.859
red.

00:00:35.859 --> 00:00:39.870
Like fire, he could not be easily contained
and never kept to just one shape.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.660
He and Odin, king of the gods, were blood
brothers, which made him basically a member

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.449
of the family no matter how much trouble he
caused.

00:00:46.449 --> 00:00:49.510
And as the god of mischief, he caused no end
of trouble.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:54.030
He also produced monstrous children, who had
their own roles to play in the mythology.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.449
He was the father of Hel, the half-withered
goddess of the underworld, and of Fenrir,

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:01.929
the giant Wolf who bit the hand off of the
god Tyr.

00:01:01.929 --> 00:01:07.300
Having once taken the form of a mare, he was
the mother of Odin's eight-legged horse, Sleipnir.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.690
As a prank, Loki once cut all of the hair
off of Thor's wife Sif.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:16.460
When he got in trouble for it, he made amends
by giving Sif new hair spun of gold, and also

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.320
commissioning the dwarves to forge Thor's
famous hammer, Mjolnir.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.340
When Loki proved too troublesome, Odin bound
him under the Earth, where a serpent constantly

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.020
drips poison on his face.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.500
He'll be released with the coming of Ragnarok,
the Norse apocalypse, in which all the gods

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.190
and monsters will fight to the death.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:40.330
Loki's first appearance in Marvel Comics was
in Journey into Mystery #85, published in

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.330
1962.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.600
This version was created by Jack Kirby and
Stan Lee, who had introduced Thor only two

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.210
issues earlier.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.050
Once Thor had become a superhero, it only
made sense to bring in Loki as a supervillain.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.360
Stan Lee freely drew what he wanted from the
Norse myths, while Kirby created a visual

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:00.810
language for Marvel's Asgard — one that
made these super-gods look unlike any Norse

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.490
people who'd ever lived, while retaining some
basic iconography.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.399
The new Loki was still slimmer than Thor and
Odin, but now he had black hair and dressed

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:10.920
in green and gold.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.420
Whereas Thor's helmet had wings, Loki's had
large horns.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.400
Instead of Odin's blood brother, Marvel Loki
was his adopted son, making him Thor's brother,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.680
and thus a more equal adversary.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.999
He relied less on shapeshifting than his mythical
counterpart, but made up for it with impressive

00:02:25.999 --> 00:02:26.999
skills at sorcery.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.609
Loki became Thor's recurring arch enemy, and
perhaps even more importantly, he was the

00:02:32.609 --> 00:02:35.290
very first villain who faced the Avengers.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.159
In fact, he accidentally brought the team
together.

00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:42.670
Attempting to mess with Thor from a distance
while imprisoned in Asgard in Avengers #1,

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:46.550
Loki manipulated the Hulk to make people think
he was on a rampage.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:51.189
That got not only Thor involved, but also
Iron Man, Ant-Man, and the Wasp.

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:55.249
When the four heroes realized Loki was the
true culprit, they teamed up with the Hulk

00:02:55.249 --> 00:02:56.550
to battle Loki.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.170
Afterwards, they decided to stay together
as a team, using their combined powers to

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.430
protect the world from threats too big for
just one hero.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:11.854
"Avengers... assemble."

00:03:11.854 --> 00:03:15.819
Supervillain or not, Loki was still Thor's
brother.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:20.069
That made their relationship much more complex
than other heroes and their archenemies.

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:24.270
With Loki, there's some part of him that loves
Thor, and knows Thor loves him back, just

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.450
as they both love their father Odin.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:31.799
On top of that, as more of a mischievous sorcerer
than an evil world-conqueror, Loki was just

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:34.969
too interesting to stay entirely a villain
forever.

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:39.510
So, in time, there were stories where he teamed
up with Thor to face greater threats.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:44.419
The most notable example was in the 1980s,
during the acclaimed Thor run by writer/artist

00:03:44.419 --> 00:03:45.419
Walt Simonson.

00:03:45.419 --> 00:03:51.390
In the culmination of a long-foreshadowed
plot, the fire giant Surtur was attacking

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:55.019
Asgard with an army of the dead, and threatening
all the realms beyond.

00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:59.319
Odin and his two sons stormed into battle
together, each with a battle cry and that

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.579
revealed their priorities in resisting Surtur.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.340
During the "Siege" crossover, Loki sacrificed
himself and died.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.459
He was then reincarnated as an adolescent
boy.

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:14.349
Far more pure of heart than his older counterpart,
Kid Loki had his own series of adventures

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:17.389
in a new volume of "Journey Into Mystery."

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:21.430
At the end of that story, Kid Loki's body
was taken over by a more amoral version of

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:26.400
the character from his previous incarnation
— although he retained the Kid Loki identity.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.800
Kid Loki went on to found a new version of
the Young Avengers, featuring the Kate Bishop

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:36.150
version of Hawkeye, as well as Wiccan, Hulkling,
Marvel Boy, and America Chavez.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.810
Over the course of that series, the other
young heroes gradually came to trust this

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:44.240
young god of mischief, even as Loki himself
struggled with whether or not he was worthy

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.240
of that trust.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.629
Late in "Young Avengers," Kid Loki is magically
aged up to around college age.

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:54.919
He remained younger than he'd previously been,
while becoming enough of an adult to interact

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:58.669
with Thor and other adult characters without
being treated like a child.

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:03.690
After the end of "Young Avengers," Loki got
his own comic, titled "Loki: Agent of Asgard."

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:09.060
The idea behind the title was that Loki, no
longer villainous but still amoral, was perfectly

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.780
suited to take on secret and sometimes ethically
suspect missions for the rulers of Asgard,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.650
like a one-god black ops team.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.270
It was a perfect premise for the character,
and led to some well-loved stories.

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:25.080
Meanwhile, the Marvel Cinematic Universe was
making Loki more popular than he'd ever been,

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.199
with tons of people who'd never read a Marvel
comic becoming big fans of the character.

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:33.720
A huge part of that popularity has to be attributed
to the work of Tom Hiddleston, the handsome

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.060
English actor who was cast in the role.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.040
Most of Hiddleston's previous acting work
was on British television, and he was largely

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.050
unknown in the United States.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:47.010
That changed with the release of "Thor" in
2011, in which Hiddleston's Loki was the primary

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.020
antagonist.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:52.199
At the beginning of the movie, Loki is presented
as an ally to his brother Thor, accompanying

00:05:52.199 --> 00:05:57.930
the thunder god and his friends on an ill-fated
trip to Jotunheim, home of the Frost Giants.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.849
Things soon break down, however, when Thor
is exiled to Earth and Loki learns he's actually

00:06:01.849 --> 00:06:04.050
of the Frost Giant race himself.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.349
As Odin enters a mystical slumber, Loki plots
to take over Asgard.

00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:12.610
To do that he has to remove Thor from the
line of succession, even if it means killing

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.610
him.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:17.370
Although he was the villain of the piece,
fans enjoyed his complicated morality as much

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.690
as his handsome face.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.699
Just as Loki was responsible for the founding
of the original Avengers in the comics, so

00:06:23.699 --> 00:06:26.910
too was Hiddleston's version in 2012's "The
Avengers."

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:31.889
In this version, Loki is wielding a mind-controlling
staff and is working in tandem with an alien

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:34.280
race in an attempt to conquer the Earth.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.810
To stop him, SHIELD brings together Thor,
Iron Man, Captain America, the Hulk, Black

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.180
Widow, and Hawkeye.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:44.570
Once again, Loki's actions lead to the formation
of Earth's greatest super-team, to his regret.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.570
"You are all of you beneath me.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.889
I am a god, you dull creature.

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:52.479
And I will not be bullied by—"

00:06:56.409 --> 00:07:02.370
2013's "Thor: The Dark World" finds Loki imprisoned
in Asgard following the events of "The Avengers."

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:07.349
When Dark Elves invade and kill Frigga, mother
of Thor and adoptive mother of Loki, Thor

00:07:07.349 --> 00:07:10.110
releases Loki to help defeat the Elves.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:14.520
While this sequel is frequently criticized,
audiences did get something they'd been wanting:

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.160
a less evil Loki.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.800
In fact, that's what Tom Hiddleston wanted
as well.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.590
In a 2013 interview with Total Film magazine,
Hiddleston explained,

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:26.960
"When I met Alan [Taylor, director of 'Dark
World'], he asked me how I thought I could

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.479
do Loki again without repeating myself and
I remembered talking with Kevin Feige when

00:07:31.479 --> 00:07:33.409
we were on the 'Avengers' promotional tour.

00:07:33.409 --> 00:07:37.810
I said, 'OK, you've seen Thor and Loki be
antagonistic for two films now.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.599
It would be amazing to see them fight side
by side."

00:07:40.599 --> 00:07:43.990
Loki's duplicity inevitably emerges at the
film's end, of course.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:48.219
The god of mischief appears to die heroically
in battle with the Dark Elves, but he later

00:07:48.219 --> 00:07:51.879
reveals himself as alive and masquerading
as Odin.

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:56.020
By taking his father's form, Loki has achieved
his ambition to rule Asgard.

00:07:57.139 --> 00:08:01.360
After appearing in Marvel movies for three
years in a row, Loki had a four-year break

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:05.319
before turning back up in 2017's "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:09.540
Upon returning to Asgard, Thor finds his brother
still impersonating Odin.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:13.499
The two go in search of the real Odin, who
has returned to Norway, the land where he

00:08:13.499 --> 00:08:15.659
once was worshiped, to die.

00:08:15.659 --> 00:08:20.159
Upon his death, the Death Goddess Hela is
freed from an ancient imprisonment.

00:08:20.159 --> 00:08:25.280
She effortlessly destroys Thor's hammer and
then sends Thor and Loki careening into endless

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.280
space.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:30.949
Loki finds himself on the planet Sakaar and
ingratiates himself to its ruler, the hedonistic

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:32.289
Grandmaster.

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:37.240
Thor soon arrives as well and is forced to
fight as a slave in the gladiatorial arena,

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.810
where his first opponent is the Hulk.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:45.130
Soon Thor and Loki team up with Bruce Banner
and a long-lost Asgardian Valkyrie to escape

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.000
Sakaar and return to Asgard to face Hela.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.930
In "Ragnarok," Loki's still not exactly trustworthy,
but he's not a villain at all anymore, and

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:57.320
ultimately proves himself a worthy ally to
his brother as the two escape the destruction

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.970
of Asgard with most of the population in a
huge ship.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.160
"I wouldn't worry, brother.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:05.589
I have a feeling that everything's going to
work out fine."

00:09:05.589 --> 00:09:08.270
This new status quo, however, would be sadly
short-lived.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:14.300
Avengers: Infinity War, released in 2018,
is the climax of the Marvel meta-story that

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.680
had been building since the first movie.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.880
It's fitting, therefore, that it begins with
Thanos invading the Asgardian ship and killing

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:21.880
Loki.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:25.560
The original Avengers villain dies a hero,
at the hands of the ultimate villain who was

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.440
secretly using Loki during the invasion of
Earth in "The Avengers."

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.519
At this point, Thanos is gathering the Infinity
Stones as part of his mission to wipe out

00:09:33.519 --> 00:09:38.100
half of all life in the universe, and none
of the Asgardians are powerful enough to stop

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:42.800
him from gaining the Tesseract, the Infinity
Stone that was at the center of that plot

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.130
in Avengers.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:48.510
Hiddleston's Loki had evolved so far by this
point that it was sad for basically everyone,

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.380
not just the Loki mega-fans, to see him strangled
to death by Thanos.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:56.790
He came so close to being a hero in his own
right, and maybe, there at the end, he was

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:57.790
one.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.500
When he turned up next, however, it was as
the villain he'd once been.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:06.639
Thanos wins at the end of "Infinity War,"
so in 2019's "Avengers: Endgame," the surviving

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:11.140
Avengers have to go back in time to recover
the Infinity Stones from various points in

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.000
history — before they were acquired by Thanos.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:18.040
As they explain before doing so, each time
they change the past, their actions create

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.079
an alternate timeline where things went differently.

00:10:21.079 --> 00:10:25.600
One of their time travel destinations is the
aftermath of the invasion in the first "Avengers,"

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.610
when Loki had been defeated and taken into
custody.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:32.211
During the confusion, Loki is able to get
his hands on the Tesseract once more, and

00:10:32.211 --> 00:10:34.620
use it to escape to parts unknown.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:38.350
What this means, of course, is that there's
a Loki out there in the Marvel multiverse

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:41.970
again, despite his death at Thanos' hands
in the main timeline.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:46.450
But what it also means is that the Loki who
now exists is one who'd never fought alongside

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.570
Thor against the Dark Elves or helped save
the other Asgardians from Hela.

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:54.800
This Loki comes directly from a time when
he was very much a villain.

